      <div type="clause" n="29">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 29</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXIII. Gif mon sweordes onlæne oðres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-3"/> esne, ⁊ he losie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, gielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.4-3"/> he hine ðriddan dæle; gif mon spere selle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, healfne; gif he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.6-2"/> horses onlæne, ealne he hine gylde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.7-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-2"/> sweordes onlæne oþres ésne, ⁊ he losige, gilde he hine ðriddan dæle; gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-2"/> spere sylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, healfne (dæl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.1"/>) hine gilde; gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-2"/> horses<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.4-2"/> læne, ealne he hine gilde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe his sweord alæne oðres ðeowan. Gyf mon sweordes onlæne oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> esne ⁊ hit losige, be ðriddan dæle he hit gylde; gyf mon spere sylle, healfne; gyf mon hors onlæne, ealne he hine gylde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="29" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui gladium prestiterit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.2"/> ad occidendum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.3"/> aliquem (homicidium), si occidatur homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.4"/>, reddat terciam partem compositionis eius; qui lanceam prestiterit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.5"/>, dimidiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.6"/> weram; qui equum prestiterit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_29.lnote.oe.7"/>, totum reddat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="44" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam þe his sweord alæne oðres ðeowan.] Gif mon sweordes onlæne oðres esne, ⁊ he losie, gielde he hine ðriddan dæle<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_29.attnote.fn.11"/>; gif mon spere selle, healfne [dæl hine gilde]<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_29.attnote.fn.12"/>; gif he horses onlæne<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_29.attnote.fn.13"/>, ealne he hine gylde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="29" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="394" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXIII} Gif mon sweordes onlæne oðres esne, ⁊ he losie, gielde he hine ðriddan dæle; gif mon spere selle, healfne; gif he horses onlæne, ealne he hine gylde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand dem Lohnknecht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_29.lnote.de.1"/> eines anderen ein Schwert leiht, und der [Knecht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.lnote.de.2"/>] entflieht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_29.lnote.de.3"/>, so zahle er ihn [dem Herrn] zu einem Drittel; wenn jemand eine Lanze giebt, (zahle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_29.lnote.de.4"/> er ihn) halb; wenn er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_29.lnote.de.5"/> ein Pferd darleiht, zahle er ihn ganz.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone lends a sword to another’s hired servant, and the [servant] runs away, let him pay for him [to the master] to the extent of a third; if someone gives a spear, (let him pay for him) half; if he lends a horse, let him pay for him in full.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="45" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone lends a sword to the servant<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_29.attnote.n.1"/> of another man, and he makes off, he [the lender] shall pay him [the owner of the servant] a third [of his value]. If he provides [the servant] with a spear, [he shall pay the owner] half [the value of the servant]. If he lends [the servant] a horse, he shall pay him [the owner] the full value [of the servant].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="403" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone lends a sword to another's servant,<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_29.whinote.n.2"/> and he runs away, he is to pay for him a third; if he gives him a spear, half; if he lends him a horse, he is to pay his full value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="395" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone lends a sword to another’s <hi rend="italic">esne</hi> and he escapes, let [the lender] pay [the lord] one third [of the <hi rend="italic">esne</hi>’s value]; if he gives a spear, half; if he lends a horse, he compensates [the lord] for all [the value of the <hi rend="italic">esne</hi>]</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond Hn</hi> 87, 1; prestabit <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond Hn 87, 1; prestabit the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> o. a. <hi rend="italic">Lond Hn; nur</hi> ho. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only o. a. Lond Hn; only ho. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. d. w. Q. e. <hi rend="italic">überspringt R;</hi> prestitit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. d. w. Q. e. skipped by R; prestitit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">diuidat <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">diuidat M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prestitit <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prestitit R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ses <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur; aus</hi> hors onl.?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ses on an erasure; from hors onl.?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oþrum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oþrum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">losige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">losige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">be ðr. d. he hine gylde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">be ðr. d. he hine gylde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon hors <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon hors Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gilde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gilde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> unfrei 1e. 5c. — ‘Einem anderen Esne’ B falsch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> unfrei 1e. 5c. — ‘to another esne’ B, wrongly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘es’ B falsch, als erstatte der Knecht dem Entleiher das verlorene Schwert. Danach Wilkins</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘it’ B, wrongly, as though the servant were to make good the lost sword to the lender. Wilkins follows this</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q lässt Ines Sinn von einem Unfreien und dessen Entlaufen unausgedrückt und zieht den Tötungszweck hinein, wahrscheinlich aus Af 19; denn auch in seinem späteren Werke verbindet er beide Stellen: Hn 87, 1. Demgemäss fordert Q für die Beihilfe nicht Teile des Sklavenpreises, sondern des Wergeldes des Erschlagenen. Waffendarleihung wird als Beihilfe (<hi rend="italic">s. Gl d.</hi> 10f.) gebüsst und gestraft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q leaves Ine’s sense, concerning an unfree man and his running away, unexpressed and brings in the purpose of killing, probably from Af 19; for in his later work too he combines the two passages: Hn 87, 1. Accordingly, for aiding, Q demands not parts of the slave’s price but parts of the wergild of the slain man. The lending of weapons is atoned for and punished as aiding (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 10f.)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Unnötiger Zusatz H’s; ‘Teil’ ergänzt Hcor.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Unnecessary addition by H; Hcor. supplies ‘part’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_29.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘man’ B. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Schwert 5; Haftung 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘one’ B. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Schwert 5; Haftung 4</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_29.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>dæle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Gif mon sweordes onlæne oðrum esne ⁊ hit losige, be ðriddan dæle he hit gylde</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">Qui gladium prestiterit ad occidendum aliquem (homicidium), si occidatur homo</hi> etc. Quad.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_29.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>gilde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">(<hi rend="italic">dæl</hi>.) H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_29.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>onlæne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gif mon horses læne</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">gyf mon hors onlæne</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_29.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Perhaps a slave rather than a servant. The word <hi rend="italic">þeowa</hi> is used in the title (cf. note to Abt. cap. 85).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_29.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">403</biblScope></bibl><label>servant</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">esne,</hi> usually an unfree servant, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> p. 393, n. 8</seg></note>
      </div>
